{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function detectPlatform(): \"mac\" | \"windows\" | \"linux\";","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/platform.ts#L18","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.ts:18"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Detects the current platform based on browser navigator properties."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Used internally to resolve platform-adaptive modifiers like 'Mod' (Command on Mac,\nControl elsewhere) and for platform-specific hotkey formatting."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"mac\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"windows\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"linux\""}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The detected platform: 'mac', 'windows', or 'linux'"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"remarks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remarks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defaults to 'linux' in SSR environments where navigator is undefined"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const platform = detectPlatform() // 'mac' | 'windows' | 'linux'\nconst modifier = resolveModifier('Mod', platform) // 'Meta' on Mac, 'Control' elsewhere","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"remarks","text":"Remarks","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction detectPlatform(): \"mac\" | \"windows\" | \"linux\";\n```\n\nDefined in: [platform.ts:18](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/platform.ts#L18)\n\nDetects the current platform based on browser navigator properties.\n\nUsed internally to resolve platform-adaptive modifiers like 'Mod' (Command on Mac,\nControl elsewhere) and for platform-specific hotkey formatting.\n\n## Returns\n\n`\"mac\"` \\| `\"windows\"` \\| `\"linux\"`\n\nThe detected platform: 'mac', 'windows', or 'linux'\n\n## Remarks\n\nDefaults to 'linux' in SSR environments where navigator is undefined\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst platform = detectPlatform() // 'mac' | 'windows' | 'linux'\nconst modifier = resolveModifier('Mod', platform) // 'Meta' on Mac, 'Control' elsewhere\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: detectPlatform\ntitle: detectPlatform\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction detectPlatform(): \"mac\" | \"windows\" | \"linux\";\n```\n\nDefined in: [platform.ts:18](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/platform.ts#L18)\n\nDetects the current platform based on browser navigator properties.\n\nUsed internally to resolve platform-adaptive modifiers like 'Mod' (Command on Mac,\nControl elsewhere) and for platform-specific hotkey formatting.\n\n## Returns\n\n`\"mac\"` \\| `\"windows\"` \\| `\"linux\"`\n\nThe detected platform: 'mac', 'windows', or 'linux'\n\n## Remarks\n\nDefaults to 'linux' in SSR environments where navigator is undefined\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst platform = detectPlatform() // 'mac' | 'windows' | 'linux'\nconst modifier = resolveModifier('Mod', platform) // 'Meta' on Mac, 'Control' elsewhere\n```\n"}
